{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1143167-intentionally-failing-die-rolls-and-powers","id":1143167,"title":"Intentionally failing die rolls (and powers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-23T00:44:20-07:00","id":1143167,"title":"Intentionally failing die rolls (and powers)","content":"So, a bit of context for this; I noticed in Demon that certain Embeds and Exploits could have advantagious effects for their dramatic failure rolls. When I asked my GM about it, he suggested that deliberately evoking the dramatic failure result of a roll be done on an exceptional success. I even made an Interlock to allow a character to substitute a dramatic failure result for a normal success (minus gaining a beat for it)...except another person later pointed out that in the base game, you can choose to intentionally fail a die roll.<br /> <br /> I've not seen errata that supports it, but I'm curious if the rules do support intentionally failing a die roll outside of conditions such as Spooked. I posted this here instead of the Demon thread because this kind of ruling affects games outside of Demon (though admitedly I've not seen many results where the Dramatic Failure can be innately useful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-23-2017, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T00:58:15-07:00","id":1143169,"title":"","content":"It's positively ancient by the standards of this iteration of the forums, but this has been covered before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=13950#post13950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can choose to dramatically fail a roll <i>if you failed the roll to begin with</i>. But if you're using the power, my assumption as ST is that you're trying to do what the Embed actually does. Want to do the dramatic failure effect more consistently? Fine, teach yourself to do it (that is, make up a new Embed or Exploit).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T01:18:27-07:00","id":1143171,"title":"","content":"Much appreciated Satchel; thank you for reposting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-23-2017, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}